## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/grunge_aurora.html
- Summary (EN): Grunge Aurora generates a pattern of leaking lines resembling an aurora display. It works as a building block for more intricate textures, such as light patterns in a night sky or water-damaged walls.
- Résumé (FR) : Grunge Aurora produit un motif de traits lumineux qui rappelle une aurore boréale, utile comme brique pour un ciel nocturne ou un mur abîmé par l'eau.

- Inputs meaning: ["size_ref: representative layer that sets the output image size and metadata"]

- Key parameters: ["Range: Amplitude scales values, Center offsets them, output spans C-A to C+A; Mask Contrast adds contrast before both", "Pattern: Element Size, Element Scale (with Per-Component Controls), Offset, Tile Size as repeat period", "Aurora: Distortion Strength (vertical distortion along X), Distortion Size (roughness of the distortion), Streak Weight (ramp weighting samples along each pixel trajectory)", "Aurora > Advanced: Maximum Steps caps distortion steps; raise it if stepping artifacts appear", "Post Processing, applied in order: Fold, Complement, Bias, Gain, Gamma, Contrast, Clamp Minimum, Clamp Maximum"]

- Caveats: ["Output can be negative or above 1; use the Clamp options", "Complement behaves as expected only for values from 0 to 1", "Fold has no effect when all values are positive", "Tile Size should match the aspect ratio of non-square images", "Post-processing Contrast is distinct from Noise Contrast on some noise nodes"]

